# 45 hotel brands: (slug, name, url, verified fact, observation 1, observation 2, slide notes [(text, fx, fy)])
# fx/fy = where the note's line points, as a fraction of the logo's visible bounds.
B=[
("marriott","Marriott","https://www.marriott.com/","J. Willard and Alice Marriott started with a root beer stand in Washington, D.C., in 1927 and opened their first hotel in 1957.","The flowing red script makes the world's largest hotel company feel personal, like a signature.","A small line underneath spells out \"hotels, resorts, suites\", so the script can stay large and expressive.",[("red emblem",0.5,0.05),("script wordmark",0.2,0.6),("hotels, resorts, suites",0.75,0.97)]),
("hilton","Hilton","https://www.hilton.com/","Conrad Hilton bought his first hotel, the Mobley in Cisco, Texas, in 1919.","An H monogram in a circle works as an app icon and on signage, while the serif name carries the heritage.","Deep Hilton blue keeps the brand calm and trustworthy across thousands of properties.",[("H monogram",0.5,0.1),("classic serif",0.2,0.6),("Hilton blue",0.85,0.6)]),
("hyatt","Hyatt","https://www.hyatt.com/","Hyatt began in 1957, when Jay Pritzker bought the Hyatt House motel next to Los Angeles International Airport.","Thin, widely spaced capitals give the name a light, modern feel.","A blue arc sweeps under the letters like a smile, adding warmth to an otherwise strict wordmark.",[("thin caps",0.12,0.3),("blue arc",0.5,0.85),("Hyatt blue",0.85,0.3)]),
("ihg","IHG Hotels & Resorts","https://www.ihg.com/","IHG became an independent company in 2003 and adopted the \"IHG Hotels & Resorts\" name and logo in 2021.","Three bold initials sit next to a two-line descriptor, so the group name is clear without a symbol.","The all-black logo lets the colourful brands it owns, like Holiday Inn and InterContinental, take the spotlight.",[("three initials",0.15,0.4),("two-line descriptor",0.8,0.25),("black only",0.8,0.85)]),
("accor","Accor","https://group.accor.com/","Paul Dubrule and Gérard Pélisson opened the first Novotel near Lille in 1967, and the group returned to the simple Accor name in 2019.","A gold A, shaped like a stylized peak, gives the group a luxurious symbol.","Spaced capitals underneath keep the wordmark quiet and premium.",[("gold A",0.5,0.25),("spaced caps",0.25,0.95),("2019 rebrand",0.85,0.9)]),
("wyndham","Wyndham","https://www.wyndhamhotels.com/","Wyndham was founded in Dallas in 1981 by real estate developer Trammell Crow.","Wide blue capitals make the name easy to read on highway signs and building tops.","A thin swoosh and a small descriptor line underneath add movement and context.",[("wide blue caps",0.2,0.3),("swoosh line",0.2,0.62),("hotels & resorts",0.85,0.92)]),
("radisson","Radisson","https://www.radissonhotels.com/","The first Radisson Hotel opened in Minneapolis in 1909, named after French explorer Pierre-Esprit Radisson.","The bold brush script feels energetic and hospitable, unlike the strict type of most chains.","A teal underline finishes the script and adds a fresh accent colour.",[("brush script",0.2,0.3),("teal underline",0.6,0.95),("explorer's name",0.85,0.3)]),
("best-western","Best Western","https://www.bestwestern.com/","M.K. Guertin founded Best Western in 1946 as a referral network of independent hotels.","The BW initials work as a compact mark, separated from the name by a thin line.","Rounded, friendly letters in deep blue make the brand feel approachable and reliable.",[("BW initials",0.08,0.3),("rounded sans",0.6,0.3),("hotels & resorts",0.7,0.9)]),
("holiday-inn","Holiday Inn","https://www.ihg.com/holidayinn/","Kemmons Wilson opened the first Holiday Inn in Memphis, Tennessee, in 1952.","The green script H recalls the brand's famous \"Great Sign\" from the 1950s and 60s roadside motels.","The friendly italic wordmark and small \"by IHG\" line connect the brand to its parent company.",[("green script H",0.5,0.15),("friendly italic",0.2,0.65),("by IHG",0.5,0.97)]),
("the-ritz-carlton","The Ritz-Carlton","https://www.ritzcarlton.com/","The brand takes its name from Swiss hotelier César Ritz, and The Ritz-Carlton Boston, opened in 1927, set the standard for the modern brand.","The lion and crown emblem gives the brand an aristocratic, almost heraldic feel.","Serif capitals joined by a hyphen keep the name formal and elegant.",[("lion and crown",0.04,0.3),("serif caps",0.5,0.3),("hyphenated name",0.7,0.9)]),
("four-seasons","Four Seasons","https://www.fourseasons.com/","Isadore Sharp opened the first Four Seasons, a motor hotel in Toronto, in 1961.","The tree symbol represents the four seasons, with leaves that suggest growth and nature.","The small caps wordmark under the tree is quiet and refined, typical of luxury hotels.",[("tree symbol",0.5,0.2),("small caps",0.2,0.9),("Toronto, 1961",0.85,0.85)]),
("st-regis","St. Regis","https://st-regis.marriott.com/","John Jacob Astor IV opened The St. Regis New York in 1904.","The ornate monogram looks like a family crest, a nod to the Astor heritage.","Widely spaced capitals next to it keep the logo balanced and formal.",[("ornate monogram",0.08,0.4),("spaced caps",0.6,0.3),("Astor heritage",0.8,0.85)]),
("waldorf-astoria","Waldorf Astoria","https://www.hilton.com/en/brands/waldorf-astoria/","The Waldorf Astoria New York opened on Park Avenue in 1931, replacing the original hotel from the 1890s.","The interlocking WA monogram is inspired by the hotel's Art Deco heritage.","The two names stack in small, soft grey capitals, which keeps the logo understated.",[("WA monogram",0.5,0.1),("stacked names",0.3,0.6),("soft grey",0.85,0.6)]),
("mandarin-oriental","Mandarin Oriental","https://www.mandarinoriental.com/","Mandarin Oriental grew from The Mandarin in Hong Kong, which opened in 1963.","The gold fan is the brand's signature symbol, linking it to its Asian roots.","Each hotel in the group has its own version of the fan, which makes the symbol collectable.",[("fan symbol",0.3,0.3),("gold",0.85,0.4),("small caps",0.5,0.92)]),
("the-peninsula","The Peninsula","https://www.peninsula.com/","The Peninsula Hong Kong opened in 1928, and it is the flagship of the Peninsula Hotels group.","Classic serif capitals give the name the feel of a grand old hotel.","A thin rule and widely spaced \"Hotels\" underneath add a finishing, formal touch.",[("classic serif",0.2,0.3),("thin rule",0.2,0.62),("spaced HOTELS",0.8,0.92)]),
("rosewood","Rosewood","https://www.rosewoodhotels.com/","Caroline Rose Hunt founded Rosewood in Dallas in 1979 with The Mansion on Turtle Creek.","Wide, heavy capitals with generous spacing give a short name a strong presence.","With no symbol, the wordmark relies entirely on proportion and spacing.",[("wide caps",0.2,0.4),("no symbol",0.6,0.2),("generous spacing",0.8,0.85)]),
("aman","Aman","https://www.aman.com/","Adrian Zecha opened the first Aman, Amanpuri in Phuket, in 1988, and aman means \"peace\" in Sanskrit.","The A's are drawn without crossbars, so the letters feel open and calm.","A small macron over the first A adds a subtle, almost spiritual detail.",[("macron",0.05,0.03),("open A's",0.4,0.5),("means \"peace\"",0.85,0.85)]),
("belmond","Belmond","https://www.belmond.com/","Orient-Express Hotels was renamed Belmond in 2014, and LVMH acquired the group in 2019.","Spaced geometric capitals look modern while still feeling refined.","The single-word name replaced the old Orient-Express branding, which belonged to a different train company.",[("spaced caps",0.2,0.4),("geometric",0.6,0.3),("LVMH-owned",0.85,0.85)]),
("sheraton","Sheraton","https://sheraton.marriott.com/","Ernest Henderson and Robert Moore founded Sheraton in 1937 in Springfield, Massachusetts.","The S inside a laurel wreath looks like a seal of quality.","The brand name famously came from an illuminated hotel sign that was too expensive to replace.",[("S in a laurel",0.3,0.4),("serif name",0.5,0.92),("crest",0.85,0.3)]),
("westin","Westin","https://westin.marriott.com/","Westin began as Western Hotels in Seattle in 1930, and the Westin name was adopted later.","Heavy, high-contrast serif letters give the name a confident, classic look.","A warm bronze colour and spaced descriptor underneath feel calm and premium.",[("heavy serif",0.2,0.3),("warm bronze",0.65,0.2),("hotels & resorts",0.5,0.92)]),
("intercontinental","InterContinental","https://www.ihg.com/intercontinental/","Pan American World Airways founded InterContinental Hotels in 1946 to house travellers on its new routes.","A gold I inside a medallion acts like a coin or a seal.","The serif capitals with a small dot recall the golden age of international air travel.",[("gold I medallion",0.5,0.2),("serif caps",0.15,0.85),("Pan Am roots",0.85,0.85)]),
("conrad","Conrad","https://www.hilton.com/en/brands/conrad-hotels/","Hilton launched Conrad as its luxury brand in 1982, naming it after founder Conrad Hilton.","The A without a crossbar gives the gold capitals a distinctive, modern twist.","The brand uses the founder's first name, which makes it feel personal and exclusive.",[("gold caps",0.15,0.3),("no crossbar A",0.65,0.3),("founder's first name",0.5,0.92)]),
("fairmont","Fairmont","https://www.fairmont.com/","The Fairmont San Francisco opened in 1907, and the brand is now part of Accor.","The large flourished F turns the wordmark into an elegant signature.","The calligraphic script suggests old-world hospitality and grand hotels.",[("flourished F",0.06,0.4),("calligraphic script",0.6,0.3),("San Francisco, 1907",0.8,0.9)]),
("kempinski","Kempinski","https://www.kempinski.com/","Kempinski is Europe's oldest luxury hotel group, with roots in Berthold Kempinski's business in Berlin.","The flowing signature script looks like a handwritten name, which feels personal.","The \"Hoteliers since 1897\" line underneath stresses the brand's long heritage.",[("long K",0.05,0.3),("signature script",0.5,0.4),("since 1897",0.6,0.95)]),
("shangri-la","Shangri-La","https://www.shangri-la.com/","Robert Kuok opened the first Shangri-La hotel in Singapore in 1971, naming it after the paradise in the novel Lost Horizon.","The gold S symbol looks like mountains reflected in water, a nod to the mythical place.","Spaced capitals and a small descriptor underneath keep the logo balanced and formal.",[("mountains in water",0.5,0.1),("spaced caps",0.2,0.65),("Lost Horizon",0.85,0.85)]),
("sofitel","Sofitel","https://sofitel.accor.com/","Accor's founders opened the first Sofitel in Strasbourg, France, in 1964.","Extremely wide letter spacing gives the short name an airy, elegant feel.","Geometric capitals keep the logo modern and very French.",[("very wide spacing",0.15,0.5),("geometric caps",0.6,0.3),("French luxury",0.85,0.75)]),
("grand-hyatt","Grand Hyatt","https://www.hyatt.com/brands/grand-hyatt","The first Grand Hyatt opened in New York in 1980, next to Grand Central Terminal.","White capitals inside a red bar make the logo look like a bold sign.","A thin vertical line separates the two words, so each one reads clearly.",[("red bar",0.05,0.3),("divider line",0.5,0.1),("white caps",0.85,0.75)]),
("w-hotels","W Hotels","https://w-hotels.marriott.com/","The first W Hotel opened in New York in 1998.","A single letter W is all the brand needs, which makes it feel confident and design-led.","The tiny descriptor underneath almost disappears, so the W does all the work.",[("single letter W",0.5,0.2),("tiny descriptor",0.3,0.85),("New York, 1998",0.85,0.85)]),
("ace-hotel","Ace Hotel","https://acehotel.com/","Alex Calderwood, Wade Weigel and Doug Herrick opened the first Ace Hotel in Seattle in 1999.","Condensed capitals in a heavy black frame look like a vintage hotel sign.","The logo feels more like a record label than a hotel brand, which fits its creative audience.",[("condensed caps",0.2,0.3),("black frame",0.97,0.5),("like a sign",0.3,0.92)]),
("edition","Edition","https://www.editionhotels.com/","Edition is a partnership between Marriott and hotelier Ian Schrager, who co-founded Studio 54.","High-contrast serif capitals look like a fashion magazine masthead.","A line cutting through the O adds one unexpected detail to an otherwise classic wordmark.",[("high-contrast serif",0.2,0.3),("cut O",0.78,0.5),("Ian Schrager",0.3,0.92)]),
("1-hotels","1 Hotels","https://www.1hotels.com/","Barry Sternlicht launched 1 Hotels, opening the first one in Miami Beach in 2015.","A giant serif 1 dominates the logo, so the brand name is a single character.","A deep green colour reflects the brand's focus on nature and sustainability.",[("giant serif 1",0.3,0.3),("deep green",0.85,0.3),("tiny HOTELS",0.5,0.97)]),
("kimpton","Kimpton","https://www.ihg.com/kimptonhotels/","Bill Kimpton opened his first boutique hotel in San Francisco in 1981.","A clean sans serif wordmark keeps the founder's name simple and friendly.","The minimal logo lets each Kimpton hotel have its own personality and design.",[("clean sans",0.2,0.4),("founder's name",0.6,0.8),("® mark",0.98,0.1)]),
("hotel-indigo","Hotel Indigo","https://www.ihg.com/hotelindigo/","IHG launched Hotel Indigo in 2004, with the first hotel in Atlanta.","The two words stack, with a large INDIGO under a smaller HOTEL.","The deep indigo blue matches the brand name, which makes it easy to remember.",[("indigo blue",0.15,0.3),("stacked words",0.2,0.7),("neighbourhood hotels",0.85,0.92)]),
("the-hoxton","The Hoxton","https://thehoxton.com/","The first Hoxton hotel opened in Shoreditch, London, in 2006.","Bold lowercase letters make the name feel relaxed and approachable.","The heavy, slightly quirky serif gives the brand a neighbourhood pub feel.",[("lowercase",0.2,0.3),("heavy serif",0.6,0.4),("Shoreditch, 2006",0.85,0.92)]),
("citizenm","citizenM","https://www.citizenm.com/","citizenM opened its first hotel at Amsterdam Schiphol Airport in 2008.","A bold red M symbol works as an icon, while \"citizen\" sits above in lowercase.","The playful lowercase name signals the brand's casual, tech-friendly style.",[("lowercase citizen",0.5,0.05),("red M",0.2,0.75),("app-ready icon",0.85,0.85)]),
("moxy","Moxy","https://moxy-hotels.marriott.com/","Marriott launched Moxy in 2014, with the first hotel at Milan Malpensa Airport.","Loopy, handwritten letters make the logo feel playful and young.","Bright magenta is unusual for a hotel brand, and it stands out instantly.",[("loopy script",0.2,0.4),("magenta",0.6,0.2),("playful",0.85,0.9)]),
("six-senses","Six Senses","https://www.sixsenses.com/","Sonu and Eva Shivdasani founded Six Senses in 1995, and IHG bought the brand in 2019.","A small pattern of dots sits above the name, like stones or seeds.","Thin, widely spaced capitals make the wellness brand feel calm and quiet.",[("dot pattern",0.5,0.3),("thin caps",0.2,0.95),("wellness brand",0.85,0.9)]),
("one-and-only","One&Only","https://www.oneandonlyresorts.com/","Kerzner International launched One&Only as its ultra-luxury resort brand in 2002.","The flowing italic script makes the name feel romantic and exclusive.","The ampersand joins the two words into one continuous signature.",[("flowing script",0.15,0.4),("ampersand",0.47,0.6),("resort brand",0.85,0.85)]),
("banyan-tree","Banyan Tree","https://www.banyantree.com/","Ho Kwon Ping and Claire Chiang opened the first Banyan Tree resort in Phuket, Thailand, in 1994.","The banyan tree illustration has trunks that look like figures, which suggests shelter and community.","Hand-drawn capitals underneath feel natural and handcrafted.",[("banyan tree",0.5,0.2),("hand-drawn caps",0.2,0.9),("Phuket, 1994",0.85,0.9)]),
("club-med","Club Med","https://www.clubmed.com/","Gérard Blitz founded Club Med in 1950, and its trident symbol dates back to the brand's early years.","Bold, rounded blue letters feel friendly and holiday-ready.","The trident next to the name is a nod to the sea and the brand's beach villages.",[("bold blue",0.3,0.4),("trident",0.95,0.3),("since 1950",0.6,0.92)]),
("atlantis","Atlantis","https://www.atlantisbahamas.com/","Sol Kerzner opened Atlantis Paradise Island in the Bahamas in the 1990s.","Wide, spaced capitals in ocean blue make the name feel grand and aquatic.","The location line underneath connects the brand to its flagship resort.",[("wide caps",0.2,0.3),("ocean blue",0.6,0.2),("Paradise Island",0.5,0.95)]),
("raffles","Raffles","https://www.raffles.com/","Raffles Hotel Singapore opened in 1887, named after Sir Stamford Raffles.","The traveller's palm illustration links the brand to its tropical Singapore origins.","Bold, spaced capitals underneath balance the detailed drawing.",[("traveller's palm",0.5,0.2),("bold caps",0.2,0.85),("Singapore, 1887",0.85,0.85)]),
("the-savoy","The Savoy","https://www.thesavoylondon.com/","Richard D'Oyly Carte opened the Savoy in London in 1889.","Thin, elegant capitals make the short name look refined and timeless.","Wide spacing gives each letter room, like the hotel's famous Art Deco interiors.",[("thin caps",0.2,0.4),("wide spacing",0.6,0.3),("London, 1889",0.85,0.85)]),
("the-plaza","The Plaza","https://www.theplazany.com/","The Plaza opened at Fifth Avenue and Central Park South in New York in 1907.","A gold crest above the name gives the hotel a regal, monumental feel.","Classic serif capitals and a small \"New York\" line underneath tie the brand to its city.",[("gold crest",0.5,0.1),("serif caps",0.2,0.8),("New York, 1907",0.85,0.95)]),
("jumeirah","Jumeirah","https://www.jumeirah.com/","Jumeirah was founded in Dubai in 1997, and its Burj Al Arab hotel opened in 1999.","Elegant serif capitals keep the logo calm, even though the brand's hotels are spectacular.","The long J extends below the line, giving the name a distinctive first letter.",[("long J",0.03,0.7),("serif caps",0.4,0.3),("Dubai, 1997",0.85,0.85)]),
]
